---
title: "Editing Modes"
---

Two alternative editing modes support specialised workflows: full row editing and batch editing.

## Full Row Editing

[Full Row Editing](./cell-editing-full-row/) makes all cells in a row editable simultaneously, giving users the impression that the record as a whole is being edited. It's well-suited to form-like workflows where fields are related and should be edited together. When a row is in edit mode, pressing {% kbd "⇥ Tab" /%} moves between editable cells; {% kbd "↵ Enter" /%} or clicking outside commits all changes; {% kbd "⎋ Esc" /%} discards them.

## Batch Editing {% enterpriseIcon /%}

[Batch Editing](./cell-editing-batch/) queues edits across multiple cells or rows without immediately writing them to your data. Changes accumulate as **pending values** and are applied in one operation when the batch is committed, or discarded entirely if cancelled.

This is useful for bulk data entry workflows, spreadsheet-like experiences, and scenarios where you need to preview changes before saving to a back end. Batch Editing is available only via the API and is compatible with the Client-Side Row Model only.
